To test the main hypothesis that an external EF can affect early-stage root infection, we first implemented the global configuration (Fig. 1A) to expose roots to nominal EFs known to cause P. palmivora zoospore electrotaxis22: 0.5 V/cm, 0.7 V/cm, and 1.0 V/cm, with the corresponding current and current density measured in the system (Table 1). After 2h exposure, when zoospore attachment and germination had occurred10, we observed the roots under a confocal microscope and calculated a zoospore-attachment index normalized to take into account variation in total zoospore numbers within each replicate:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
