We compared the two configurations using nominal EFs to generate comparable currents of ~ 250 μA and ~ 530 μA (Table 2). In both cases (weak and strong currents) the global EF performed better in reducing zoospore attachment to the roots, as confirmed by confocal imaging (Fig. 4A,B). Interestingly, while the local EF performed about the same at weak and strong currents, the global EF further improved its effect at stronger currents, occasionally achieving zoospore-free roots (Fig. 4B).Table 2
